<div class="content"><section class="hero"><span class="badge">DAILY AI REPORT · 11:00 PM</span><h1>Your whole day.<br>One clear direction.</h1><p>A daily review connecting your training, movement, nutrition, and recovery—with a practical plan for tomorrow.</p><div class="meta">FRIDAY, 16 OCTOBER 2026 · ASIA/KOLKATA (IST)<br>Today’s saved records through 11:00 pm · Includes rest days</div></section>
<div class="metrics complete-only">${metric('Movement','8,420','of 10,000 steps')}${metric('Training','54 min','1 workout · 19 sets')}${metric('Nutrition','2,180 kcal','of 2,400 kcal target')}${metric('Sleep','6 h 20','last night · target 8 h')}</div>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><h2>The big picture</h2><span class="badge">CONNECTED DAILY REVIEW</span></div><div class="card"><div class="takeaway complete-only"><h3>A solid training day. Give recovery more room.</h3><p>You completed your lower-body session and logged 8,420 steps. Sleep was below your saved target, soreness was 5/10, and your logged energy and protein intake were below plan. Consider those signals together before increasing tomorrow’s training load.</p></div><div class="takeaway missing-only"><h3>A useful start, with a few gaps.</h3><p>Your workout and steps are available, but dinner and your recovery check-in are missing. Nutrition totals are partial, and there is not enough information to recommend a training increase or assess full-day intake.</p></div><div class="signals complete-only"><span>Training completed</span><span>Sleep below target</span><span>Protein 22 g below plan</span></div><div class="missing-message">Incomplete day: 2 meals logged; dinner not confirmed. No recovery check-in. Missing values stay unknown and are excluded from confident conclusions.</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><h2>01 · Training & movement</h2><span class="muted" style="font-size:11px">All sessions, one day</span></div><div class="card"><h3>Legs B · Posterior chain</h3><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin:0 0 18px">6 exercises completed · 19 working sets · 54 minutes</p><div class="routine"><div><strong>8,420</strong><small>Daily steps / 10,000</small></div><div><strong>2,625 kg</strong><small>Logged lifting volume</small></div><div><strong>8 / 10</strong><small>Last deadlift set RPE</small></div></div><details><summary>View exercises & logged sets</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Exercise</th><th>Recorded sets · kg × reps</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Deadlift</td><td>37 × 8 · 38 × 8 · 37.5 × 10</td></tr><tr><td>Goblet squat</td><td>15 × 8 · 15 × 8 · 15 × 8</td></tr><tr><td>Walking lunge</td><td>7.5 × 8 · 7.5 × 8 · 7.5 × 8</td></tr><tr><td>Hip thrust</td><td>20 × 8 · 20 × 10 · 20 × 16</td></tr><tr><td>Calf raise</td><td>10 × 8 · 10 × 10 · 10 × 10 · 15 × 10</td></tr><tr><td>Hanging knee raise</td><td>8 · 8 · 8 reps · bodyweight</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p class="note">Lifting volume uses recorded load × reps; bodyweight work is listed separately. Rest days show movement and recovery without a workout requirement.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><h2>02 · Full-day nutrition</h2><span class="badge complete-only">4 MEALS LOGGED</span><span class="badge missing-only">PARTIAL INTAKE</span></div><div class="card complete-only"><div class="two"><div>${nutrient('Energy','2,180 kcal','2,400',91)}${nutrient('Protein','128 g','150 g',85)}${nutrient('Carbohydrate','264 g','280 g',94)}</div><div>${nutrient('Fat','66 g','80 g',83)}${nutrient('Fiber','26 g','30 g',87)}${nutrient('Water','2.3 L','3.0 L',77)}</div></div><div class="meal-list"><strong>Meals included</strong><br>08:30 · Breakfast &nbsp; / &nbsp; 13:15 · Lunch &nbsp; / &nbsp; 17:00 · Snack &nbsp; / &nbsp; 21:10 · Dinner<br>Includes saved food add-ons and logged supplements. No supplements logged in this example.</div><p class="note">Targets shown are illustrative saved personal targets. Food composition values are estimates; logged meals do not prove that every food was captured. Calories may differ slightly from rounded macros.</p></div><div class="card missing-only"><h3>Full-day totals unavailable</h3><p class="muted">Breakfast and lunch are saved. Dinner is unconfirmed. Partial totals would be labeled here; no daily nutrient shortfall is inferred.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><h2>03 · Micronutrient coverage</h2><span class="muted" style="font-size:11px">Known values only</span></div><div class="card"><p class="note" style="margin-top:0">Food entries may not contain every nutrient. Unknown composition is never counted as zero. These sample targets are for layout review.</p><div class="table-wrap complete-only"><table><thead><tr><th>Nutrient</th><th>Logged estimate</th><th>Saved target</th><th>Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody>${microRows.map(r=>'<tr>'+r.map(v=>`<td>${v}</td>`).join('')+'</tr>').join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="missing-only muted">Daily coverage is unavailable until meal logging is complete. Unknown nutrient values remain visible as unknown.</p><p class="note">Available nutrients would appear here, including food add-ons and supplements. A day below an intake target does not establish a deficiency.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><h2>04 · Recovery & check-in</h2><span class="muted complete-only" style="font-size:11px">Latest saved check-in · 9:30 pm</span></div><div class="card complete-only"><div class="routine"><div><strong>6 h 20 min</strong><small>Sleep · quality 6/10</small></div><div><strong>5 / 10</strong><small>Soreness · legs</small></div><div><strong>6 / 10</strong><small>Energy</small></div></div><div class="routine" style="margin-top:20px"><div><strong>4 / 10</strong><small>Stress</small></div><div><strong>58 bpm</strong><small>Resting heart rate</small></div><div><strong>None logged</strong><small>Pain flags</small></div></div><p class="note">Mood 7/10 · Motivation 7/10 · HRV not recorded · Weight 72.4 kg (morning)<br>Daily hydration is shown once in nutrition; steps are shown once in movement.</p></div><div class="card missing-only"><h3>Recovery check-in not logged</h3><p class="muted">Sleep, soreness, energy, stress, and pain status are unknown. No recovery score is invented.</p></div></section>
